  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 15.2, p. 260. Book: EFL 151.5, BFL 0, NA -1.2886 (F/0.6), GIH 5.61 (HFOV=3.27), PTZ/F -0.5468, VL 405.64, OD 9049.37 (MAG -0.016). Glass: BK7 entered as N-BK7; CAF entered as CAF2 (calcium fluoride); K5 entered as N-K5. The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 1, surface 1, the rear (long-conjugate) end of the objective, where a microscope objective's aperture stop usually sits (the table has no plane stop row). The book image lies at the back of the K5 layer (BFL 0); a zero-thickness dummy surface inside the K5 ends the table so the image stays in the immersion medium. The book prints sa 423.0 on surface 10; 42.3 (as on the surfaces either side) is used. The table is printed above the caption of Figure 15.2 on p. 260. The book's EFL 151.5 is n' f with n' = 1.515; with the K5 index 1.522 the model gives 152.2 (its focal length in air is 100.0). BFL here is the paraxial image distance for the finite object.",
